# Points at the RESERVED ngrok domain.
#
# This was deliberately left unset for a long time, because lib/api.ts can
# derive the backend from the Expo dev server's own hostUri -- whatever LAN
# address this laptop has right now -- and scanning the QR on any network then
# finds the backend with nothing to edit.
#
# The reason it was unset no longer holds. That note warned that ngrok free
# issues a NEW random URL every restart, so the moment the tunnel died every
# request failed -- login, alerts and the password reset alike. The domain
# below is a RESERVED ngrok domain, stable across restarts, and is already the
# one baked into eas.json's preview profile and the backend's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS. A pinned static domain is what makes this safe to set.
#
# Set because the phone reaches the backend through the tunnel rather than
# directly: mobile data, or a network that blocks client-to-client traffic.
#
# NOTE for the dev client: EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined by Metro at BUNDLE time,
# and a dev client loads its bundle from `npm start` on this laptop -- so
# changing this line and restarting the dev server re-points the app with NO
# new build. Only standalone (preview/production) builds bake it on EAS, which
# is why eas.json carries its own copy.
#
# Unset this (comment it out) to go back to LAN auto-detection.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://turkey-semifinal-dullness.ngrok-free.dev/api
